Publication maps858 historical path records (850 manifest entries plus8 manifest/freeze objects) to471 unique public byte objects, with one synthetic1911-byte KDBX carrier retained locally by digest.27 public objects can reuse existing exact history snapshots, leaving444 new inert blobs. Original exact manifests and all negative raw/source records remain intact via explicit path→blob maps; no recursive history recopy is required. Public paths contain no .local segment. Raw records intentionally retain synthetic test passwords and local Windows username/path metadata; the source author copyright email is vendor attribution. No claim of universal secret/personal-data absence is made.

## Reproduce the proposed current-layout selection

After root installs the reviewed sources and path-only adapters, the prospective selection is79 groups: retained history41 + new recycle27 + boundary5 + confirmation2 + controls4. This publication plan has not executed that selection. Root must record the actual current-source result, real UI acceptance and shared suite separately. Existing legacy app/KDBX tests remain additional regression coverage.

Use Windows, Node24.16.0, Windows PowerShell/.NET and the authenticated local KeePass2.61.1 assembly. REA_KEEPASS_EXE overrides the default repository-local acquisition path. The test-only helper checks the release before process launch and assembly load; the runtime never uses it. All files/passwords are owned synthetic fixtures. Adapted tests write detailed observations only to Studio .local or owned temporary directories; future test runs must not mutate apps/results. Child output is bounded1MiB and ordinary child deadline30 seconds, with5-second host cleanup. Descendant isolation and hard fingerprint-I/O preemption are not claimed.
